<%# What the footer's loop sheet holds: one card per loop that is being worked
    right now, and a sentence when there is none.

    A loop is not a thing this conversation can watch the way it watches a
    turn: its progress is a file on disk, written by a run in a worktree of its
    own. So each card states the four facts that answer "where did it get to?"
    -- how many iterations of how many it has spent, what it has cost, what is
    left of its budget, and when it last moved -- and nothing else. The goal is
    cut to one line because a card is a glance, and the whole of it is on the
    tooltip.

    The rows are drawn on the page and then again by the poll in _loop_sheet,
    which is why nothing here talks to the store: it is handed the rows
    (see Web::Loops#loop_rows) and only places them. -%>
<% if loops.empty? -%>
  <p class="usage-note"><%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.empty")) %></p>
<% else -%>
  <ul class="loop-rows">
<% loops.each do |loop| -%>
    <li class="loop loop-<%= h(loop[:status]) %>">
      <div class="loop-head">
        <span class="loop-id"><%= h(loop[:id]) %></span>
        <span class="loop-status"><%= h(I18n.t(loop[:status_key])) %></span>
      </div>
      <span class="loop-goal" title="<%= h(loop[:goal]) %>"><%= h(loop[:goal]) %></span>
      <span class="loop-facts">
        <%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.iterations", done: loop[:iterations], max: loop[:max_iterations])) %>
        · <%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.tokens", used: num(loop[:tokens]))) %>
        · <%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.remaining", left: num(loop[:remaining]), total: num(loop[:max_tokens]))) %>
        · <%= h(I18n.t("web.loops.updated", when: dur(loop[:age_seconds]))) %>
      </span>
    </li>
<% end -%>
  </ul>
<% end -%>
